# Domain Documentation Rules

Read `docs/context/CONTEXT.md` and relevant ADRs before changing an affected domain area.

Update Context only for verified terminology, concept boundaries, relationships, and business invariants that future work will need. Do not add current task progress, debugging notes, speculative meeting statements, code history, or technical decisions that belong in an ADR.

When evidence conflicts with Context or an ADR, report the conflict explicitly instead of silently rewriting project truth.
